# Copy to `.env`.

# Direct portal scoring sink (all sink-routed portals; see the README's
# "Supabase sink" section). Use the self-hosted Supabase API base and its
# anon key; artifacts are private and can only be inserted by anon.
SCORING_SUPABASE_URL=http://rekrutmen-supabase-a4b9d1-122-49-230-39.sslip.io
SCORING_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
SCORING_SUPABASE_BUCKET=scrape-artifacts

# Service-role key for the two service-only surfaces: the
# scrape.glints_verification code hand-off table (no anon grants) and the
# private session object glints/session/current.json in the bucket (anon is
# insert-only and cannot read or overwrite). Runtime secret — deployment env
# only. Without it the scraper still works, but a Glints device-verification
# interstitial cannot be passed and a verified session is not persisted
# across container restarts.
SCORING_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=

# Glints employer credential login (src/portalLogin.ts + src/glints.ts).
# Runtime secrets: set them in the deployment environment only — never commit
# values, and never put them in glints.json. When the injected session from
# glints.json is missing or expired the scraper logs in with these and keeps
# the refreshed session in memory; glints.json's cookies are just an optional
# warm-start. Login attempts are capped per process (2 consecutive failures,
# then a long backoff) so a wrong password cannot loop into a lockout.
#
# From an untrusted device (the server) Glints follows the credential submit
# with a "Verifikasi diri Anda" device-verification interstitial. The scraper
# then requests the EMAIL code, opens a row in scrape.glints_verification
# (needs SCORING_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY above), and logs
# GLINTS_VERIFICATION_CODE_NEEDED; a human writes the emailed code into that
# row within 10 minutes and the scraper completes the verification, then
# persists the now-trusted session to the bucket so restarts reuse it. Code
# emails are capped at one per 30 minutes via the row timestamps.
GLINTS_EMAIL=
GLINTS_PASSWORD=

# Additional Glints employer accounts (src/glints.ts's resolveGlintsAccounts):
# declare each one as an entry in glints.json's "accounts" array —
#   { "id": "second-brand", "target_company": "..." }
# — then set that account's own credential pair here, following the same
# naming the default account's GLINTS_EMAIL/GLINTS_PASSWORD above uses: the
# account id uppercased with "-" turned into "_", inserted between GLINTS and
# EMAIL/PASSWORD. Every configured account needs its own pair, or the server
# refuses to start a run that would touch it. Run a specific account with
# `glints:<id>` (e.g. `glints:second-brand` / `glints:second-brand-continuous`);
# plain `glints` / `glints-continuous` keeps running every configured account,
# one at a time.
# GLINTS_SECOND_BRAND_EMAIL=
# GLINTS_SECOND_BRAND_PASSWORD=

# Portal scraper retries (src/retry.ts). A failed Playwright run is retried
# from scratch with exponential backoff until it succeeds or the attempt
# budget runs out.
SCRAPER_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
SCRAPER_RETRY_BASE_DELAY_MS=30000
SCRAPER_RETRY_MAX_DELAY_MS=300000
SCRAPER_RETRY_FACTOR=2
SCRAPER_RETRY_JITTER=true
SCRAPER_INTERVAL_MS=300000

# Viewer AI proxy (src/viewer.ts). Upstream API key for the /api/ai/* proxy
# behind the dashboard's PageAgent chat panel. Either name works.
NINE_ROUTER_KEY=your-9router-api-key

# Google Sheet sync (src/googleSheetsSync.ts). Mirrors each portal's
# scrape.portal_vacancies/portal_candidates rows into a "Vacancies"/
# "Candidates" tab after a successful scrape_runs cycle (src/server.ts).
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID plus exactly one of the two credential shapes
# below are required together; anything missing disables the sync entirely
# (no guessing, no partial writes) — a fresh checkout runs exactly as before.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID=

# Credential shape 1: a service account (preferred for a deployed server —
# the JSON key travels with the container's env, no local file path needed).
# The full JSON key of a Google Cloud service account (Sheets API enabled on
# its project), as one line — runtime secret, deployment env only, never
# commit the real value. The sheet itself must be shared with that service
# account's client_email as an Editor, or every write fails with a 403.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# Credential shape 2: an authorized_user OAuth refresh token (for an
# operator's own Google account instead of a service account — e.g. when no
# service account has been provisioned yet). Takes priority over shape 1 only
# when GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON is unset. The token and the OAuth
# client's own client_secret each come from EITHER an inline JSON env var
# (preferred for a deployed container — one env var, no volume mount, the
# same shape GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON already uses) OR a local file
# path (for an operator-managed credential outside the repo). Only paths ever
# reach a log line; file/inline contents (refresh token, client secret,
# minted access token) never do.
#   GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN_JSON        inline token JSON (preferred for Dokploy)
#   GOOGLE_TOKEN_PATH                 — or a path to the token file
#   GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS    — alias for GOOGLE_TOKEN_PATH
#   GOOGLE_SHEETS_CLIENT_SECRET_JSON inline client_secret JSON (Dokploy)
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_PATH         — or a path to client_secret_*.json
# The token file must contain refresh_token; client_id/client_secret too if
# it already embeds them (Google ADC's authorized_user shape) — otherwise
# they come from the client_secret input (Cloud Console's downloaded
# client_secret_*.json shape, under "installed" or "web"). The account the
# token belongs to needs edit access on the sheet, the same as a service
# account would. GOOGLE_SHEETS_SCOPES only affects the service-account flow's
# token request (a refresh_token grant keeps whatever scopes the original
# consent already granted); defaults to the spreadsheets-only scope.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_TOKEN_JSON=
GOOGLE_TOKEN_PATH=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_CLIENT_SECRET_JSON=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET_PATH=
GOOGLE_SHEETS_SCOPES=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets,https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive

# CV access on the Candidates tab. Decided by the captain 2026-10-28:
# "scrapview_link" is the default (ON) — a stable link to the viewer's own
# GET /cv/:portal/:candidateId (src/viewer.ts), which mints a fresh Supabase
# signed URL on each click and redirects, the same resolve-on-click behavior
# scrapview's own UI already uses. The cell itself never expires and never
# carries a raw storage key or a baked-in signed URL. Needs SCRAPVIEW_BASE_URL
# (the viewer's public base URL) — if unset, cv_link cells are left blank
# with a warning rather than failing the sync.
# Other values, kept for flexibility/testing: "off" (no cv_link column at
# all) · "object_key" (the raw, non-expiring storage key, not a clickable
# link by itself) · "signed_url" (mints a Supabase signed link directly into
# the cell on every sync — goes stale after the TTL below until the next
# sync; needs SCORING_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY above).
GOOGLE_SHEETS_CV_LINK_MODE=scrapview_link
GOOGLE_SHEETS_CV_LINK_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS=3600
SCRAPVIEW_BASE_URL=https://scrapview.aryahanif.xyz

# One-shot, manually-run catch-up that mirrors every portal's existing
# scrape.* rows into the sheet right now, instead of waiting for each
# portal's next scrape cycle — for populating a sheet that predates the sync.
# Verifies its own row counts against Supabase and exits non-zero on a
# mismatch. Never run automatically; `npm run sheets:backfill` once the
# credential above is confirmed working.
